From 1196a6d65b71156ba5e884f03ef9dee33710b22e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua <jhollis175@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:17:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Profile management (#42): validation, tests, recruiter view

Builds on the profile/resume-delete work in feature/profile-and-resume-management.

Server
- profileController: validate every editable field (type, length, required),
  normalize skills (trim, drop blanks and case-insensitive duplicates, max 30),
  only accept http(s) links (adds https:// when missing, blocks javascript:),
  allow editing name, return 400 for bad input and 500 for server errors
- Keep job postings' company name in sync when a recruiter renames their company
- Recruiters now receive the applicant's profile (bio, location, phone, skills,
  links) when listing applications
- Remove a duplicate deleteResume from applicationController that referenced
  Applicant and fs without importing them (the routed one is in resumeController)

Client
- Profile page: name (required), read-only email, length limits, skill chips,
  server error vs success messages, form refreshes from saved values,
  Back goes to /dashboard
- Applicant dashboard: shows headline/location, or a prompt to fill the profile
- Recruiter dashboard: Profile link
- Applicants panel: shows skills, links (http(s) only) and bio

Tests
- tests/profile.test.js and tests/resumeDelete.test.js (23 cases with node:test,
  no MongoDB needed); tests/helpers.js and the npm test script are identical to
  the testing-maxime branch so the two merge cleanly

